  "style": {
    "id": "chromatography",
    "name": "Chromatography",
    "description": "Paper chromatography on a bright daylight lab bench: a white filter-paper strip hangs from a binder clip into a short glass jar with a little clear solvent, beside a steel rule, in front of a pale blue-grey tiled wall; a felt pen dots black ink near the bottom, the damp solvent front climbs the paper (square-root-of-time wicking on a speeding time-lapse clock) and the black dot stretches and splits into blue, magenta and yellow bands, each travelling at its own fixed fraction of the front and widening as it goes; the strip is lifted out and hung on a rack beside two finished strips with different band sets. The strip is one shader: code-baked fibre texture, darker damp region with a tide line, and Gaussian dye bands that subtract light per RGB channel (overlaps go dark, separated dyes show their colour). Clean white paper on blue-grey tiles, cool steel and glass, saturated dye colours.",
